HI-TECH College Integrated Digital Academic & Certification Platform
Complete User Portal, Roles, Duties, Features, Events, Properties & Permissions Specification
The platform should have a complete role-based portal system in which every user has their own dashboard, menu, responsibilities, records, notifications, events, actions and permissions.

The system must not give every user the same dashboard. Each account should display only the features and information relevant to that user's position at HI-TECH College.

Core principle: Every user must know:

What they can view.

What they can create.

What they can edit.

What they can approve.

What they can reject.

What they can upload.

What they must do daily, weekly, monthly and per term.

What events and activities concern them.

What records they are responsible for.

Who supervises them and who receives their reports.

The platform will use a centralized RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) and permission-based authorization system, with additional restrictions based on department, campus, class, course, assigned students and organizational hierarchy.

