An ICT Administrator may also be an Institution Administrator.

An Examination Officer may also be an authorized Examiner.

A Principal may hold an authorized institutional approval role.

The system should support:

Primary role.

Secondary roles.

Temporary roles.

Acting appointments.

Delegated permissions.

Role expiry.

Department restrictions.

Campus restrictions.

Programme restrictions.

Class and unit restrictions.

Users must not gain unrestricted privileges simply because they hold multiple roles.

For sensitive operations, permissions should be calculated from the exact resource and action, and conflicts between roles must be resolved using explicit policies.

