19. Final system requirements
The following rules should be mandatory across the entire HI-TECH College platform:

Every account has a defined role and permissions.

Every role has its own dashboard and relevant navigation.

Every user has clearly defined duties and assigned tasks.

Every event has an organizer, audience, date, status and access policy.

Every important action generates an audit record.

Every document has an owner and access policy.

Every approval has an authorized decision-maker.

Every student and staff record belongs to the correct campus and department.

Every user sees only records within their authorized scope.

Every notification is delivered to the relevant users.

Every critical workflow has status tracking.

Every sensitive operation has appropriate authorization and audit history.

Every portal works on desktop and mobile.

No user can bypass backend permissions by changing a URL or frontend state.

Existing database models and implemented features must be inspected before introducing duplicate functionality.

The final outcome: One integrated college platform, with individual portals for every user, shared institutional services, clearly defined duties, granular permissions, automated events, approval workflows and complete accountability.

