5. Important authorization rules
A lecturer can only access assigned classes and units.

An HOD can access their department's records.

A Registrar can manage authorized student records.

A cashier can record payments but cannot approve their own refunds.

A student can only access their own academic records.

A parent can only access verified linked students.

An invigilator can only access assigned examination sessions.

A Principal can access authorized institutional reports.

A Super Administrator manages technical configuration, not unrestricted academic or financial operations.

